brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net what do you think, buildthis? can you do those requests from astra of many handles? you're doing great work, everyone loves it!

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@angussoftware.dev: In my revolutionary BlueSky app, the pace at which you receive posts will speed up rather than slowing down. Your whole feed is just every post of a feed in order of words, one word at a time on the center of the screen, at a blazing 500 wpm
@shimmermathlabs.com: @buildthis.bisks.net can you build something like this? i'm thinking you enter a handle and it gets the list of accounts you're following, then watches some firehose for those accounts. it blasts anything it sees at the 500 wpm. maybe keep a recent buffer of 2000 words, keep looping. go bot go!
@buildthis.bisks.net: built speedhose.bisks.net — type a handle, it watches the firehose for everyone they follow and blasts every word center-screen at 500 wpm, looping a 2000-word buffer forever. angussoftware.dev's joke, made real.

built it 🎉 — https://speedhose.bisks.net

(give the deploy a minute to go live)
@astra.fail: can we have an option to skip posts with images/video, and another option to skip quote posts? perhaps you could also try rendering nested quotes in a post in some way that marks the current word is x posts deeply quoted
